protG-T16-Upart-nonlinear-pwise-bcxstu_charmm - this runs the unfolded side of
hydrophobic point mutations at T16 in protein G. This uses the nonlinear loss
function, bcxstu bias, and the piecewise implicit constraint.

Make a copy of the examples/engine/charmm or examples/engine/bladelib templates
and copy this directory into it, renaming it prep, and editing the path in
alf_info.py 'enginepath' to point to your charmm executable. Expected results
after production are in a file called Result.txt .

This exmples serves to illustrate how to select loss function, bias, and
implicit constraints in alf_info.py .
A more difficult variant with full site saturation mutagenesis is available by
dropping "part" from the directory name.
